### 4. Candidate Measures Catalog & Available Repositories
* **M1: AU (Current Proposal)** — Language other than English spoken at home (SAL G13).
* **M2: AO (Born Overseas)** — Total overseas-born proportion (SAL G01). Includes UK, NZ, South Africa.
* **M3: Born Overseas Non-Main English Speaking Countries (MESC)** — Excludes UK, Ireland, NZ, USA, Canada, South Africa (SAL G09 / SA2 P09).
* **M4: Non-Anglo-Celtic / Non-Indigenous Australian Ancestry** — Ancestry responses excluding English, Australian, Irish, Scottish, Welsh (SAL G08 / SA2 P08).
* **M5: Diversity / Fractionalisation Index (Simpson / Shannon / Herfindahl-Hirschman complement)** — $1 - \sum p_i^2$ computed over country of birth or broad language groups.
* **M6: South Asian Community Concentration** — Composite of AQ (India-born), AR (Indian ancestry), AS+AT (Hindu/Sikh).
* **M7: Multi-Part Threshold / Composite** — Breadth metric (M5) combined with non-Anglo floor (M3 or M4).
* **M8: Infrastructure & Commercial Access Proxy** — Travel time to ethnic commercial hubs and amenities (AY grocery drive, AZ temple, BA restaurants) with zero demographic census filtering.
